* Candidate bridge-local overcurrent path. KELVIN is measured at the shunt,
* with its negative sense terminal at this bridge's logic reference.
.subckt LEG_CURRENT_OK KELVIN VLOGIC OK params: VOS=0 TCOMP=4n FILTER=1.1n
Rinput KELVIN sense 100
Rbias VLOGIC sense 1k
Cfilter sense 0 {FILTER}
Rref_high VLOGIC reference 6.98k
Rref_low reference 0 1k
Cref reference 0 100p
* Smooth comparator transfer, then a delay at the logic threshold.
Bcomp compare 0 V={v(VLOGIC)*0.5*(1+tanh((v(reference,sense)-VOS)/2m))}
Rcomp compare OK 1k
Ccomp OK 0 {TCOMP/(1000*0.69314718)}
.ends LEG_CURRENT_OK

* READY reports latched health without depending on PEER combinationally.
* Peer loss during RUN clears the latch. With RUN low both sides can arm
* while establishing the link. Both comparator outputs also mask EN directly.
.subckt BRIDGE_LOCAL_SHUTDOWN OK_A OK_B PG ARM RUN UPSTREAM PEER READY EN params: TLOGIC=6n
Bdata data 0 V={3.3*(v(RUN)<1.65)}
Breset reset 0 V={3.3*(v(OK_A)<1.65 || v(OK_B)<1.65 || v(PG)<1.65 || (v(RUN)>1.65 && v(PEER)<1.65))}
Ainputs [data ARM reset] [d arm_d reset_d] local_adc
.model local_adc adc_bridge(in_low=1.5 in_high=1.8)
Alatch d arm_d NULL reset_d latched NULL local_dff
.model local_dff d_dff(ic=0 clk_delay=5n reset_delay=5n)
Aoutput [latched] [armed] local_dac
.model local_dac dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=3.3 out_undef=0 t_rise=2n t_fall=2n)
Bready READY 0 V={3.3*(v(armed)>1.65 && v(OK_A)>1.65 && v(OK_B)>1.65 && v(PG)>1.65)}
Bpermit drive 0 V={3.3*(v(READY)>1.65 && v(RUN)>1.65 && v(UPSTREAM)>1.65 && v(PEER)>1.65)}
Rlogic drive EN 1k
Clogic EN 0 {TLOGIC/(1000*0.69314718)}
.ends BRIDGE_LOCAL_SHUTDOWN
